{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880122",
      "title": "Building \"reactive\" Objects",
      "lectureOrder": 289,
      "videoOrder": 256,
      "sourceHash": "55fe7743b71e134c392176a096ecce86a56f863e3fea781f63027fac3a197e78",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.42,
          "end": 4.06,
          "en": "So now we introduced the ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.06,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "which creates reactive values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "Which are values watched by Vue where changes are picked up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.71,
          "en": "to be reflected in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.71,
          "end": 14.87,
          "en": "Now, let's add a second value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.87,
          "end": 16.96,
          "en": "Let's say, besides the username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.96,
          "end": 19.833,
          "en": "we also wanna output the age year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.71,
          "end": 25.19,
          "en": "So for that, we can simply create a uAge constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.19,
          "end": 30.19,
          "en": "for example, and a second ref, with a number, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.42,
          "end": 35.42,
          "en": "And now here, I also expose age here in my object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 37.58,
          "en": "and I'm using age as a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.58,
          "end": 39.983,
          "en": "because I'm using age here in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.84,
          "end": 42.093,
          "en": "And the value for age is uAge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.11,
          "end": 48.462,
          "en": "And if we do that, we also see the age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.462,
          "end": 51.41,
          "en": "And of course we could now also change the age year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.41,
          "end": 53.87,
          "en": "in our timer if we want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.87,
          "end": 57.64,
          "en": "We can assign a new value after two seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.64,
          "end": 60.17,
          "en": "so that if we reload after two seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.17,
          "end": 62.863,
          "en": "both the name and the age change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 67.81,
          "en": "Now since we have two pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.81,
          "end": 71.23,
          "en": "name and age, which kind of belong together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.23,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "we could also consider grouping them together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 78.4,
          "en": "So here, instead of creating two refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.4,
          "end": 82.97,
          "en": "with two individual values, we could create a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.97,
          "end": 87.01,
          "en": "constant, and create a ref here which holds an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.01,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "And in an object we have a name, Maximilian",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 92.613,
          "en": "and we have a age, 31.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.7,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "So now we still have a reactive value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "but now it's a object where we grouped the data together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 101.243,
          "en": "instead of having two separate values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.7,
          "end": 105.44,
          "en": "Now we could expose the username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.44,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "by getting it from user.value.name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 112.84,
          "en": "Keep in mind, user is a ref therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.84,
          "end": 114.31,
          "en": "it has a value property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.31,
          "end": 117.19,
          "en": "and the value holds the actual value we stored here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.19,
          "end": 119.66,
          "en": "so the object with the name property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.66,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "And here we have user.dot.value.age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "and here in setTimeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "instead of changing these two individual values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 133.1,
          "en": "we now set user.value.name equal to Max",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.53,
          "end": 136.683,
          "en": "and set user.value.age equal to 32.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.9,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "And if we save that and reload, we see Maximilian and 31,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 146.51,
          "en": "but after two seconds, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.51,
          "end": 148.503,
          "en": "The data doesn't update here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 152.6,
          "en": "Well, there is a reason for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.6,
          "end": 156.65,
          "en": "When you create a ref with the ref function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.65,
          "end": 159.67000000000002,
          "en": "you get an object, Vue gives you an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.67000000000002,
          "end": 164.67000000000002,
          "en": "We can see this if we console.log it here with console log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.32,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "if I reload, that's our ref object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "and there we got this value property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 173.31,
          "en": "in which we actually got such a proxy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.31,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "You might note this proxy from the behind the scenes module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 178.313,
          "en": "we had earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 181.74,
          "en": "We also have a getter and a setter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.74,
          "end": 184.34,
          "en": "on this entire ref object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.34,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "With those, Vue keeps track of read and write access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 192.22,
          "en": "to the value property so that if you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.22,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "access user.value and you assign a brand new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 198.753,
          "en": "Vue is able to pick up this change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.97,
          "end": 204.97,
          "en": "But in addition, if you pass an object as a value to ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.36,
          "end": 210.07999999999998,
          "en": "that object is also wrapped by a proxy so that Vue is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.07999999999998,
          "en": "even able to keep track of internal changes in that object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.32999999999998,
          "end": 218.93,
          "en": "So for example here, when you drill into the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.93,
          "end": 222.123,
          "en": "and you assign a new name and age, as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.57999999999998,
          "end": 225.61,
          "en": "Nonetheless, as you also could see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.61,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "Vue was not able to update the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 230.48,
          "en": "even though I'm just telling you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.48,
          "end": 233.2,
          "en": "that it would pick up those changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.2,
          "end": 237.96,
          "en": "The problem is, how we pass that to our template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 241.81,
          "en": "Here we also drill deeply into this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.81,
          "end": 246.01,
          "en": "with user dot value, we access the object stored in our ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.01,
          "end": 248.99,
          "en": "and then the name and the age properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.99,
          "end": 251.43,
          "en": "And that's the problem we'll have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.43,
          "end": 254.55,
          "en": "name and age, these properties in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.55,
          "end": 258.46,
          "en": "the values of name and age so all of those properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.46,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "are just regular strings and numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 265.84,
          "en": "These are not reactive values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.84,
          "end": 269.72,
          "en": "So therefore, whilst Vue will indeed theoretically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.72,
          "end": 273.22,
          "en": "be possible to tell that something changed about user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.22,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "it does not understand that we're in the end exposing user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 282.05,
          "en": "to our template because we're drilling into user like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.05,
          "end": 286.71,
          "en": "So all it sees is that we expose a string and a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 286.71,
          "end": 290.3,
          "en": "And since it doesn't track those specific values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 290.3,
          "end": 292.613,
          "en": "it's not detecting any changes there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 294.47,
          "end": 299.47,
          "en": "Now one thing we could do here, is we could provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 299.47,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "the entire user object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 307.8,
          "en": "So our user ref under a user key to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 309.853,
          "en": "and output that there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 311.07,
          "end": 315.08,
          "en": "If I for example add a paragraph here temporarily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 315.08,
          "end": 318.6,
          "en": "I can output user now because we're exposing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.6,
          "end": 322.79,
          "en": "this user key here and if I do so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 322.79,
          "end": 325.33,
          "en": "indeed you will see my object here and you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 325.33,
          "end": 328.03,
          "en": "it also changed after two seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.03,
          "end": 328.973,
          "en": "Here you go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.05,
          "end": 335.997,
          "en": "And therefore, we could of course also output user.name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 336.90999999999997,
          "end": 339.49,
          "en": "or user.age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 339.49,
          "end": 342.9,
          "en": "So drill into this object here in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 342.9,
          "end": 345.15999999999997,
          "en": "and now it would work if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 345.15999999999997,
          "end": 347.2,
          "en": "after two seconds it updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 347.2,
          "end": 349.84000000000003,
          "en": "Because now I still drill into this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 349.84000000000003,
          "end": 354.48,
          "en": "but only in the template, I pass the raw object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 354.48,
          "end": 358.02,
          "en": "the raw ref object to the template here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 358.02,
          "end": 360.893,
          "en": "in my return statement of the setup function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 361.82,
          "end": 363.94,
          "en": "And that is what matters to Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 363.94,
          "end": 367.63,
          "en": "With that it gets this raw ref object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 367.63,
          "end": 372.12,
          "en": "It has all the reactivity that's in this object and it knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 372.12,
          "end": 374.81,
          "en": "when we assign a new value and it knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 374.81,
          "end": 376.62,
          "en": "that we're using this in a template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 376.62,
          "end": 380.33,
          "en": "so then it goes ahead, finds the places in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 380.33,
          "end": 384.053,
          "en": "where we use this object and updates that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 386.71,
          "end": 390.02,
          "en": "And that is how we would use ref correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 390.02,
          "end": 394.303,
          "en": "with an object instead of separate values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.58,
          "end": 398.7,
          "en": "But if you are working with an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 398.7,
          "end": 401.87,
          "en": "there actually is a better alternative to ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 401.87,
          "end": 405.46,
          "en": "Instead of using ref, which you could use like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 405.46,
          "end": 408.89,
          "en": "And of course, by the way, you could now delete all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.89,
          "end": 411.65999999999997,
          "en": "Exposing just the user would be enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 411.65999999999997,
          "end": 416.09000000000003,
          "en": "but instead of using ref, you can now also import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 416.09000000000003,
          "end": 420.703,
          "en": "the reactive function, which is all provided by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 422.07,
          "end": 425,
          "en": "Reactive is a bit like ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 425,
          "end": 428.24,
          "en": "but it's explicitly made for objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 428.24,
          "end": 432.17,
          "en": "So now instead of ref, we call reactive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 432.17,
          "end": 435.473,
          "en": "and you still pass your object to reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 436.725,
          "end": 441.49,
          "en": "But where ref worked with any kind of value, strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 441.49,
          "end": 446.49,
          "en": "numbers and objects, reactive only works with objects here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 447.05,
          "end": 450.173,
          "en": "So you must pass an object to reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 451.32,
          "end": 454.19,
          "en": "And now reactive does one important thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 454.19,
          "end": 457.27,
          "en": "It doesn't wrap this with an extra object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 457.27,
          "end": 461.01,
          "en": "which has a value prop, which then points at your value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 461.01,
          "end": 464.71,
          "en": "Instead it makes this object which you passed to reactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 464.71,
          "end": 468.01,
          "en": "reactive by wrapping it into a proxy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 468.01,
          "end": 470.86,
          "en": "so that you can still work with this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
